  "text": "I can understand why you would feel angry. It's natural to want to make your own choices and decisions, especially when it comes to something as important as friendships.\n\nWhen I was in a similar situation, I tried to explain to my mom that I understood her concerns, but I also needed to have some freedom to choose my own friends. I told her that I would be responsible and make good choices, and that I would always be there for her and our family.\n\nIt took some time and effort, but eventually, my mom started to understand and trust me more. She realized that I was capable of making good decisions and that I would always prioritize our family's values and well-being.\n\nIt might not be the same for you, but I want you to know that you're not alone in this. Many people have to deal with similar situations, and it's okay to feel angry and frustrated. But it's also okay to try to communicate with your mom and find a way to work through your differences.\n\nWhat do you think? Would you like to try talking to your mom about this, or is there something else that's been on your mind that you'd like to talk about?",
